In an effort to realize control and treatment techniques for VOCs, many types of materials, including activated carbon, nanoparticles, nanocomposites, graphene, zeolites, metal oxides, carbon nanotubes, and metal organic frameworks (MOFs) have been developed and employed extensively in various applications. In general, sorbent materials are known to offer great solutions for many applications due to their excellent features, including porous and crystalline structures with high surface areas. However, most commonly utilized sorbent materials also suffer from a number of drawbacks in terms of practicality. In the case of zeolites, a lack of thermal and mechanical stability limits the field of their application [14]. Consequently, many efforts have been made to modify their structures to improve adsorption capacity. The concept
